<text x="370.84" y="624.205" size="5.08" layer="94">Ethernet</text>
<text x="490.22" y="617.22" size="3.81" layer="94">EEPROM</text>
<text x="459.74" y="623.57" size="5.08" layer="94">MAC Address</text>
<text x="495.3" y="613.41" size="2.1844" layer="94">16 Kbit</text>
<text x="494.03" y="609.6" size="2.1844" layer="94">(2048x8)</text>
<text x="381" y="528.955" size="2.1844" layer="214">The PHY is setted up as follows:</text>
<text x="381" y="525.78" size="2.1844" layer="214">MODE: All capable(10/100Base).</text>
<text x="388.62" y="522.605" size="2.1844" layer="214">Auto-negotiation enabled.</text>
<text x="388.62" y="519.43" size="2.1844" layer="214">MII Configuration</text>
<text x="388.62" y="516.255" size="2.1844" layer="214">SMI address: 0x01</text>
<text x="485.14" y="575.945" size="1.4224" layer="94" ratio="15">I2C Address: 0xA0</text>
<text x="332.74" y="398.78" size="1.778" layer="97">ToDo: Ferrite (select w/high Z at high F,
low Z at low F). Try to block everything
&gt;1MHz or so.</text>
<text x="332.74" y="383.54" size="1.778" layer="97">C3: Use 1uF to filter high frequency noise,
or 10uF if lower frequency noise is present</text>
<text x="332.74" y="388.62" size="1.778" layer="97">NOTE: For the best power on/off pop
performance, the amplifier should be set in the
shutdown mode prior to power on/off operation
(set SD low to power down the amp).</text>
<text x="300.99" y="494.03" size="6.4516" layer="94">Audio</text>
<text x="172.72" y="439.42" size="1.778" layer="94">2*100nf removed as 
they're somewhere else</text>
